  "tagline": "Sacred Hawaiian dance of chant, gesture and storytelling",
  "profile": "Hula is the traditional dance of Native Hawaiians, integrating chanted poetry (mele/oli), rhythmic movement and a vocabulary of hand gestures that depict nature, emotions and narrative (Wikipedia). Many hula are religious performances dedicated to deities; dancers learning sacred hula were ritually secluded under the protection of Laka, goddess of hula, in a halau (Wikipedia). American Protestant missionaries arriving in 1820 denounced and nearly suppressed hula; King David Kalakaua revived it in the late 19th century (New World Encyclopedia). Forms range from ancient hula kahiko to modern hula auana.",
